From: Artem Bambalov <artembambalov1993@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ccodec: a codec that could not be configured is an error

CCodec::allocate() asks the config to initialize itself, and when that
fails it writes a warning and carries on:

    status_t err = config->initialize(mClient, comp);
    if (err != OK) {
        ALOGW("Failed to initialize configuration support");
        // TODO: report error once we complete implementation.
    }

The TODO is upstream's own, and the consequence is not a degraded codec but
a dead process. initialize() builds mParamUpdater, so a failure leaves it
null, and the very next thing anyone does with the codec walks into it:

    F libc: Fatal signal 11 (SIGSEGV), fault addr 0x4 in tid (NDK MediaCodec_)
      #00 libsfplugin_ccodec.so CCodecConfig::getReflectedFormat(...)
      #01 libsfplugin_ccodec.so CCodecConfig::getConfigUpdateFromSdkParams(...)
      #03 libsfplugin_ccodec.so CCodec::configure(...)

On this board that is not a corner case. SystemUI decodes the interface
sounds through Codec2 while it starts, so an initialize() failure kills
SystemUI, which is a persistent process, so it starts again, decodes again
and dies again -- a loop fast enough that the screen only flickers and the
device cannot be used at all. Nothing in that picture names the cause: the
log fills with crashes in a media library and with binder replies that
cannot be delivered to a process which is, by then, already dying.

Report the failure instead. The same function three lines above already
shows the shape for it, for a component that could not be created: set the
state to RELEASED, drop the lock, call onError. A codec whose configuration
support never came up is no more usable than one that was never created,
and the callers -- SoundPool here -- handle "no codec" perfectly well.

This does not fix whatever made initialize() fail; it stops that failure
from taking the process with it, which is also what makes the real cause
observable, since a system restarting SystemUI twice a second cannot be
measured.

---
diff --git a/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp b/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp
--- a/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp
+++ b/media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodec.cpp
@@ -654,9 +654,19 @@
     // initialize config here in case setParameters is called prior to configure
     Mutexed<Config>::Locked config(mConfig);
     status_t err = config->initialize(mClient, comp);
     if (err != OK) {
         ALOGW("Failed to initialize configuration support");
-        // TODO: report error once we complete implementation.
+        // mocha: and then stop, rather than continue with a half-built
+        // config. initialize() is what creates mParamUpdater, so carrying on
+        // means the next caller dereferences it and the process dies -- which
+        // on a persistent process is a boot loop rather than a failed codec.
+        config.unlock();
+        Mutexed<State>::Locked state(mState);
+        state->set(RELEASED);
+        state.unlock();
+        mCallback->onError(err, ACTION_CODE_FATAL);
+        state.lock();
+        return;
     }
     config->queryConfiguration(comp);

